REM RESTORE DATA with no LOCAL DATA: the manual says "DATA not LOCAL"
REM (54); the Z80 version 5.4 does nothing when another LOCAL frame (here
REM ON ERROR LOCAL, or a LOCAL variable) is on top: RESLO2's POP IX
REM overwrites the "nothing restored" flag
10 PROCa:PROCb:PRINT "end"
20 END
30 DEF PROCa:LOCAL X
40 ON ERROR LOCAL PRINT ERR;" ";REPORT$:ENDPROC
50 RESTORE DATA:PRINT "PROCa: no error"
60 ENDPROC
70 DEF PROCb
80 ON ERROR LOCAL PRINT ERR;" ";REPORT$:ENDPROC
90 RESTORE DATA:PRINT "PROCb: no error"
100 ENDPROC
RUN
